          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without number.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to Joseph were born two sons before the years of famine came: which Asenath the daughter of Poti-pherah priest of On bore to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph called the name of the first-born Manasseh: For God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "said he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", hath made me forget all my toil, and all my father's house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the name of the second called he Ephraim: for God hath caused me to be fruitful in the land of my affliction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the seven years of plenteousness that was in the land of Egypt, were ended.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.54",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.54",
      "verse": 54,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the seven years of dearth began to come, according as Joseph had said: and the dearth was in all lands; but in all the land of Egypt there was bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.55",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.55",
      "verse": 55,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when all the land of Egypt was famished, the people cried to Pharaoh for bread: and Pharaoh said to all the Egyptians, Go to Joseph; what he saith to you, do.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.56",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.56",
      "verse": 56,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the famine was over all the face of the earth; and Joseph opened all the store-houses, and sold to the Egyptians; and the famine became severe in the land of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.41.57",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.41.57",
      "verse": 57,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all countries came into Egypt to Joseph to buy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "corn",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; because the famine was distressing in all lands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
